    "knowledge_point": "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix",
    "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -4 & 14 \\\\ 8 & 2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 11 & -1 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-26 & 0 & -10 & -10 \\\\ 30 & 0 & 0 & 22 \\\\ -52 & 0 & -12 & -32 \\\\ 11 & -1 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary row operations \n\nI. ${R}_{1}:=…$\n\nII. ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{4}$\n\nIII. ${R}_{3}:=…$\n\neach of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{4},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary row operations?",
    "worked_solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries above ${a}_{42}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -4 & 14 \\\\ 8 & 2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 11 & -1 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-3{R}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-26 & 0 & -10 & -10 \\\\ 8 & 2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 11 & -1 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-26 & 0 & -10 & -10 \\\\ 30 & 0 & 0 & 22 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 11 & -1 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-5{R}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-26 & 0 & -10 & -10 \\\\ 30 & 0 & 0 & 22 \\\\ -52 & 0 & -12 & -32 \\\\ 11 & -1 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-3{R}_{4}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-5{R}_{4}.$",
